<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brigham Young</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1801">1801</a>–<a href="/years/1877">1877</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brigham Young was the second president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-jesus-christ-of-latter-day-saints">Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints</a>, leading it from 1844. He organised the migration of the Mormons from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illinois">Illinois</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salt-lake-valley">Salt Lake Valley</a> in 1847 and directed the settlement of much of the Great Basin. He headed the proposed State of Deseret and was the first governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/utah-territory">Utah Territory</a> from 1850 to 1858.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brigham-young.jpg" alt="Brigham Young" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles William Carter (1832 - 1918) Details on Google Art Project · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charles_William_Carter_-_Brigham_Young_-_Google_Art_Project_(3x4_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
